    "A2"
  ],
  "slug": "a-mouse-without-confidence",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/2990_a-mouse-without-confidence.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "There was a little mouse in the forest who thought it looked unimpressive and had few abilities. It felt it was at the very bottom of the animal world. So it went to the mountain god and begged him again and again to turn it into a cat. The mountain god agreed. But just a few days after becoming a cat, the little mouse had a new problem: cats were afraid of dogs! It went back to the mountain god and asked to be turned into a dog. Then it discovered that dogs were afraid of wolves, so it hurried back and asked to become a wolf. After changing into many different animals, the little mouse finally became an elephant. Now all the animals were afraid of it, and it was delighted. But after a while, it discovered that what elephants feared most was mice. Suddenly, the animal it admired most was a mouse again, so it ran back to beg the mountain god once more...",
    "There is no use envying others, because everyone has weaknesses. Only by believing in yourself can you find the courage to defeat your rivals."
  ],
  "english_full": "There was a little mouse in the forest who thought it looked unimpressive and had few abilities. It felt it was at the very bottom of the animal world. So it went to the mountain god and begged him again and again to turn it into a cat. The mountain god agreed. But just a few days after becoming a cat, the little mouse had a new problem: cats were afraid of dogs! It went back to the mountain god and asked to be turned into a dog. Then it discovered that dogs were afraid of wolves, so it hurried back and asked to become a wolf. After changing into many different animals, the little mouse finally became an elephant. Now all the animals were afraid of it, and it was delighted. But after a while, it discovered that what elephants feared most was mice. Suddenly, the animal it admired most was a mouse again, so it ran back to beg the mountain god once more...\n\nThere is no use envying others, because everyone has weaknesses. Only by believing in yourself can you find the courage to defeat your rivals.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "В ле́су жила́ не́большая мышка, кото́рая ду́мала, что она́ вы́глядит не́впечатляюще и име́ет не́сколько способностей. Она́ чувствовала, что она́ на́ходится в са́мом ни́зком положении среди жи́вотных. Поэ́тому она́ пошла́ к бо́гу горе́ и па́ки и па́ки у́моляла его́ преврати́ть её́ в ко́шку. Бог го́ры согласи́лся. Но всего лишь не́сколько дне́й по́сле того́, как она́ ста́ла ко́шкой, у неё́ появи́лась нова́я пробле́ма: ко́шки боя́лись соба́к! Она́ верну́лась к богу горе́ и спра́шивала, чтобы её преврати́ли в соба́ку. Тогда́ она́ откры́ла, что соба́ки бо́ятся волков, поэ́тому она́ спеши́ла обратно и спра́шивала, чтобы стать волком. По́сле то́го, как она́ измени́лась во мнóжество других жи́вотных, мышка на́конец ста́ла сло́ном. Теперь все жи́вотные бо́ялись её́, и она́ была́ восто́рженная. Но по́сле неко́торого вре́мени она́ откры́ла, что бóльше всего сло́ны бо́ятся мышек. Вдруг жи́вотное, которым она́ наи́большее восхища́лась, снова́ стало мышкой, поэтому она́ побежа́ла обратно, чтобы на́зад у́молять бога горе́ ещё раз...",
    "Нет смысла зави́довать другим, потому что у ка́ждого е́сть свои́ слабости. Толька́ лишь веря́ в себя́, ты сможешь на́йти сме́лость победи́ть своих сопе́рников."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "V lésu zhilá nébol'shaya mýshka, kotoráya dúmala, chto oná výgladit névpechatlyayushche i iméyet néskol'ko sposobnostey. Oná chuvstvovala, chto oná nakhoditsya v sámom nízkom polozhenii sredi zhivotnykh. Póetomu oná poshlá k bógu góry i páki i páki úmoljala egó prevratít' yéye v kóshku. Bog góry soglasilsya. No vsego lish' néskol'ko dney pósle tógo, kak oná stála kóshkoy, u neyé poyavilás' nováya problemá: kóshki boyalis' sobak! Oná vernulás' k Bogu góry i sprashívala, chtoby yéyo prevratít' v sobaku. Togdá oná otkrýla, chto sobaki boyatsya volkov, póetomu oná speshila obratno i sprashívala, chtoby stat' volkom. Pósle tógo, kak oná izmenilas' vo mnózhestvo drugikh zhivotnykh, mýshka nakonéts stála slónom. Téper' vse zhivotnye boyalis' yéy, i oná bylá vostorzhennaya. No pósle nekotorýkh vremeni oná otkrýla, chto bólshe vsego slóny boyatsya mýshok. Vdrug zhivotnoe, kotorim oná naíbol'shoye voskhíshalas', snová stalo mýshkoy, poetomu oná pobezhala obratno, chtoby nazad úmol'javat' Boga góry yeshcho raz...",
    "Net smysla zavídovat' drugim, potomu chto u kázhdogo yest' svoí slabosti. Tol'ko lish' verýa v sebyá, ty smozhesh' naíti smélost' pobedít' svoikh sopérniki."
  ],
